## 2. [Query Library](#2-query-library)  

- Purpose: Queries within the Query Library drive [dashboards](#10-dashboards) via [searches](#8-searches), [scheduled searches](#6-scheduled-searches) via [alert queries](#8-2-alert-queries), and [playbooks](#7-playbooks).  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/querylibrary/querylibrary.html>)  
    - Updating a query in the library updates dependent dashboards and scheduled searches automatically.  
    - Total queries: ***418***  
        - [8.1 Dashboard Searches](#8-1-dashboard-searches): ***372***  
        - [8.2 Alert Queries](#8-2-alert-queries): ***42***  

***  

## 3. [Naming Schema](#3-naming-schema)  

- Purpose: The use of a standard naming convention enables users to quickly understand the function, severity, and context of a query or component. This approach facilitates efficient identification, reuse, and troubleshooting without ambiguity.  
- *QueryType - MongoDB - Atlas - {Logtype} - {Logsubtype} - Name [Visualization - if any]*  
- Examples:  
    - Templates: *Template - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Category [chart]*  
    - Searches: *Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Tag [numbercard]*  
    - Alert Queries: *AlertQuery - MongoDB Atlas - MongoDB Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Critical Atlas Alert [Visualization - if any]*  

***  

## 4. [Resources](#4-resources)  

- Purpose: Resources allow users to store persistent data for use in searches.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/resources/resources.html>)  
- Total: ***6***  

#### 4.1. [Lookups](#4-1-lookups)  

- Purpose: Lookup Resources are used by the *lookup* module to perform data enrichment and translation off of a static lookup table stored in a resource.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/search/lookup/lookup.html>)  
- Total: ***6***  
    - mongodb-atlas-categories: Tag-to-category and subcategory lookup used by the generated MongoDB Atlas General Overview dashboard.  
    - mongodb-atlas-admin-api-endpoints: Documented Atlas Admin API endpoint-to-tag routing catalog using angle-bracket placeholders.  
    - mongodb-atlas-admin-api-fields: Documented Atlas Admin API fields used by the MongoDB Atlas autoextractors. Array source paths use .[]. notation.  
    - mongodb-atlas-alert-statuses: Documented MongoDB Atlas alert status values used by searches and dashboards.  
    - mongodb-atlas-alert-risk-catalog: Atlas event and alert risk lookup using documented Atlas alert and org event type names.  
    - mongodb-atlas-event-types: Documented eventTypeName values from the Atlas Admin API Return Events from One Organization eventType parameter.  

***  

## 5. [Alerts](#5-alerts)  

- Purpose: Alerts notify you of potential nefarious actions that took place within and/or against your environment by tying dispatchers and consumers together.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/alerts/alerts.html#alerts>)  
- Total: ***0***  

#### 5.1. [Dispatchers](#5-1-dispatchers)  

- Purpose: Dispatchers generate events. A typical dispatcher would be a scheduled search that runs on an interval; every result returned by a scheduled search is considered an event.  
    - Dispatchers = [Scheduled Searches](#6-scheduled-searches)  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/alerts/alerts.html#adding-dispatchers>)  
- Total: ***42***  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alert Configurations - Disabled Atlas Alert Configuration [table]: Detects Atlas alert configurations that are disabled, reducing monitoring coverage.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alerts - Open Atlas Search Node Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas Search alerts for mongot OOM, stopped replication, throttling, and failed index builds.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alerts - Open Backup or Data Protection Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts for failed snapshots, stale snapshots, failed restores, delayed oplog backup capture, or backup compliance policy disablement.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alerts - Tracking Critical Atlas Alert [table]: Detects tracking Atlas alerts for critical outage, exposure, disk, backup, replication, and threshold events before they become fully open incidents.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Critical Atlas Alert Configuration Defined [table]: Detects Atlas alert configurations for high-impact events so coverage can be audited and compared against expected baseline.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - OAuth Audit Event Observed [table]: Detects documented MongoDB Atlas OAuth audit events including client, secret, authorization, token, and consent activity.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Critical Atlas Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts for infrastructure outage, public exposure, replication, disk, search, backup, and resource policy failures.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Security Posture Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts that indicate degraded security posture, missing MFA, exposed hosts, disabled UI access controls, or expiring service account secrets.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Threshold or Rate Limit Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts for metric threshold, space threshold, request-rate, billing, or usage-spike conditions.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Billing Spike [table]: Detects organization billing change events over configured thresholds.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Locked Suspended or Temporarily Activated [table]: Detects suspicious organization lock, suspension, temporary activation, or linked-organization changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization MFA Posture Weakened [table]: Detects organization-level MFA posture alerts or MFA requirement changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Role or Federation Change [table]: Detects organization role changes, role mapping changes, federation setting changes, and organization membership restriction changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Service Account Secret Risk [table]: Detects expired or expiring organization service account secrets and maximum secret validity changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization UI or Public API Access List Change [table]: Detects organization UI IP access list disabling/enabling and public API access-list policy changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Service Account Event Observed [table]: Detects MongoDB Atlas service account lifecycle, role, secret, group-assignment, and access-list events from the Atlas events endpoints.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Cloud Backups - Backup Failure Status [table]: Detects backup snapshot records with failed, canceled, expired, or fallback failure statuses.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - Cluster Client Log Redaction Disabled [table]: Detects clusters where client log redaction is disabled.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - Cluster Paused [table]: Detects clusters in a paused state.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - Cluster Unsafe Protection Settings [table]: Detects clusters with point-in-time restore, termination protection, or client-log redaction disabled.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - MongoBleed Affected MongoDB Version Observed [table]: Detects MongoDB Server versions affected by CVE-2025-14847 / MongoBleed in cluster inventory. Atlas was patched by MongoDB, but this flags any reported affected version for review.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Custom Database Roles - Dangerous Custom Database Role Action [table]: Detects custom database roles granting dangerous administrative or destructive actions.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Database Users - High Privilege Database User [table]: Detects Atlas database users with broad administrative MongoDB roles.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Network Access - Temporary Network Access Entry [table]: Detects temporary Atlas network access entries with deleteAfterDate set.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Network Access - World Open Network Access Entry [table]: Detects Atlas network access list entries open to the Internet.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Organization Users - Organization Owner User Present [table]: Detects organization users with owner role assignments for review.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Organization Users - Pending or Invited Organization User [table]: Detects organization users with invited or pending membership states.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Programmatic API Keys - High Privilege API Key [table]: Detects programmatic API keys with owner/admin-style roles.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Alert Configuration Tampering [table]: Detects project activity where alert configurations are changed, disabled, enabled, or deleted.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - API Key Lifecycle or Permission Change [table]: Detects Atlas API key creation, deletion, project membership changes, role changes, description changes, or access-list inheritance changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Atlas Log Download [table]: Detects MongoDB, mongot, or BI Connector log downloads from Atlas.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Backup Control Plane Change [table]: Detects backup compliance disablement, restore requests, snapshot deletion, retention changes, schedule updates, and key backup credential changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Cloud Provider Access Credential Change [table]: Detects AWS IAM role, Azure service principal, or GCP service account changes used for Atlas cloud provider access.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Custom Database Role Lifecycle Change [table]: Detects MongoDB custom database role creation, deletion, or update events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Database User Lifecycle Change [table]: Detects MongoDB database user creation, deletion, update, or X.509 certificate creation/revocation events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Maintenance Control Weakened [table]: Detects maintenance deferral, protected hours changes, or maintenance auto-defer changes that can affect patch cadence.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - MongoDB Employee Support Access [table]: Detects MongoDB employee SSH sessions or temporary infrastructure access bypass events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Network Permission Entry Change [table]: Detects Atlas project network permission entries being added, removed, or updated.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Observability Export Disabled or Changed [table]: Detects S3, OTel, or host external log export changes that could reduce monitoring coverage.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Project Security Checkup Degraded [table]: Detects project events indicating security checkup failures, exposed hosts, or security checkup alert configuration changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Resource Policy Violation or Change [table]: Detects resource policy creation, deletion, modification, or violation events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts - High Privilege Service Account [table]: Detects service accounts with owner/admin-style roles.  

#### 5.2. [Consumers](#5-2-consumers)  

- Purpose: Consumers process and respond to events. A typical consumer would be a flow that sends an email to an administrator, or opens a ticket in the ticketing system. Each consumer runs once per event.  
    - Consumers = [Flows](#6-1-flows)  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/alerts/alerts.html#defining-a-consumer>)  
- Total: ***1***  
    - Flow - MongoDB Atlas - Email Alerts: Detects when a Scheduled Search has fired and will email the email address input at $MONGODB\_ATLAS\_ALERT\_RECIPIENT from $MONGODB\_ATLAS\_ALERT\_SENDER.  

***  

