    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Programmatic API Keys - High Privilege API Key [table]: Detects programmatic API keys with owner/admin-style roles.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Alert Configuration Tampering [table]: Detects project activity where alert configurations are changed, disabled, enabled, or deleted.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - API Key Lifecycle or Permission Change [table]: Detects Atlas API key creation, deletion, project membership changes, role changes, description changes, or access-list inheritance changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Atlas Log Download [table]: Detects MongoDB, mongot, or BI Connector log downloads from Atlas.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Backup Control Plane Change [table]: Detects backup compliance disablement, restore requests, snapshot deletion, retention changes, schedule updates, and key backup credential changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Cloud Provider Access Credential Change [table]: Detects AWS IAM role, Azure service principal, or GCP service account changes used for Atlas cloud provider access.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Custom Database Role Lifecycle Change [table]: Detects MongoDB custom database role creation, deletion, or update events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Database User Lifecycle Change [table]: Detects MongoDB database user creation, deletion, update, or X.509 certificate creation/revocation events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Maintenance Control Weakened [table]: Detects maintenance deferral, protected hours changes, or maintenance auto-defer changes that can affect patch cadence.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - MongoDB Employee Support Access [table]: Detects MongoDB employee SSH sessions or temporary infrastructure access bypass events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Network Permission Entry Change [table]: Detects Atlas project network permission entries being added, removed, or updated.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Observability Export Disabled or Changed [table]: Detects S3, OTel, or host external log export changes that could reduce monitoring coverage.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Project Security Checkup Degraded [table]: Detects project events indicating security checkup failures, exposed hosts, or security checkup alert configuration changes.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Resource Policy Violation or Change [table]: Detects resource policy creation, deletion, modification, or violation events.  
    - ScheduledSearch - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts - High Privilege Service Account [table]: Detects service accounts with owner/admin-style roles.  

#### 6.1. [Flows](#6-1-flows)  

- Purpose: Flows provide a no-code method for developing advanced automations in Gravwell.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/flows/flows.html>)  
- Total: ***1***  
    - Flow - MongoDB Atlas - Email Alerts: Detects when a Scheduled Search has fired and will email the email address input at $MONGODB\_ATLAS\_ALERT\_RECIPIENT from $MONGODB\_ATLAS\_ALERT\_SENDER.  

***  

## 7. [Playbooks](#7-playbooks)  

- Purpose: Playbooks are hypertext documents within Gravwell which help guide users through common tasks, describe functionality, and record information about data in the system.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/playbooks/playbooks.html>)  
- Total: ***2***  
    - MongoDB Atlas Kit - Overview: Overview of the items included in the MongoDB Atlas Kit.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Kit - Readme: A toolkit for interacting with MongoDB Atlas data.  

#### 7.1. [Files](#7-1-files)  

- Purpose: Gravwell users can upload small files for use in playbooks, as cover images for kits, etc. Typically, these files are created or selected at the point of use: via a picker in the playbook editor, in the kit builder, etc.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/files/files.html>)  
- Total: ***0***  

***  

## 8. [Searches](#8-searches)  

- Purpose: These queries within the Query Library drive [dashboards](#10-dashboards) to quickly view MongoDB Atlas data in an easily digestible format or [scheduled searches](#6-scheduled-searches) to ultimately feed [alerts](#5-alerts).  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/querylibrary/querylibrary.html>)  
- Total: ***418***  
    - Dashboard Search Total: ***376***  
    - Alert Query Total: ***42***  

