    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Count by Roles [chart]: This displays a chart of all Roles (roles) values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Count by Roles [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all Roles (roles) values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Count by Secret ID [chart]: This displays a chart of all Secret ID (secretId) values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Count by Secret ID [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all Secret ID (secretId) values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Rare Client ID [numbercard]: This displays the bottom Client ID (clientId) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Rare Name [numbercard]: This displays the bottom Name (name) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Rare Roles [numbercard]: This displays the bottom Roles (roles) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Top Client ID [numbercard]: This displays the top Client ID (clientId) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Top Name [numbercard]: This displays the top Name (name) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Top Roles [numbercard]: This displays the top Roles (roles) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Total Events [chart]: This displays a chart of all MongoDB values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts Overview - Total Events [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all MongoDB events by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Category & Subcategory [chart]: This displays a chart of all MongoDB Category & Subcategory values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Category & Subcategory [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all MongoDB Category & Subcategory values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Category [chart]: This displays a chart of all MongoDB Category values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Category [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all MongoDB Category values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Subcategory [chart]: This displays a chart of all MongoDB Subcategory values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Subcategory [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all MongoDB Subcategory values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Tag [chart]: This displays a chart of all MongoDB Tag values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Tag [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all MongoDB Tag values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Database Users Overview - Rare Group ID [numbercard]: This displays the bottom Group ID (groupId) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Database Users Overview - Count by Group ID [numbercard]: This displays a numbercard of all MongoDB Group ID (groupId) values by count. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Database Users Overview - Top Group ID [numbercard]: This displays the top Group ID (groupId) during the specified timeframe. 
    - Search - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Database Users Overview - Count by Group ID [chart]: This displays a chart of all Group ID (groupId) values by count. 
- Naming Schema: *Search - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Count by Tag [numbercard]*  

#### 8.2. [Alert Queries](#8-2-alert-queries)  

- Purpose: These queries within the Query Library drive [scheduled searches](#6-scheduled-searches) which ultimately feed [alerts](#5-alerts).  
- IMPORTANT: If you need to update or tune, this is where you perform that action.  
- Total: ***42***  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alert Configurations - Disabled Atlas Alert Configuration [table]: Detects Atlas alert configurations that are disabled, reducing monitoring coverage.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alerts - Open Atlas Search Node Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas Search alerts for mongot OOM, stopped replication, throttling, and failed index builds.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alerts - Open Backup or Data Protection Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts for failed snapshots, stale snapshots, failed restores, delayed oplog backup capture, or backup compliance policy disablement.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Alerts - Tracking Critical Atlas Alert [table]: Detects tracking Atlas alerts for critical outage, exposure, disk, backup, replication, and threshold events before they become fully open incidents.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Critical Atlas Alert Configuration Defined [table]: Detects Atlas alert configurations for high-impact events so coverage can be audited and compared against expected baseline.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - OAuth Audit Event Observed [table]: Detects documented MongoDB Atlas OAuth audit events including client, secret, authorization, token, and consent activity.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Critical Atlas Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts for infrastructure outage, public exposure, replication, disk, search, backup, and resource policy failures.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Security Posture Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts that indicate degraded security posture, missing MFA, exposed hosts, disabled UI access controls, or expiring service account secrets.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Threshold or Rate Limit Alert [table]: Detects open Atlas alerts for metric threshold, space threshold, request-rate, billing, or usage-spike conditions.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Billing Spike [table]: Detects organization billing change events over configured thresholds.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Locked Suspended or Temporarily Activated [table]: Detects suspicious organization lock, suspension, temporary activation, or linked-organization changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization MFA Posture Weakened [table]: Detects organization-level MFA posture alerts or MFA requirement changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Role or Federation Change [table]: Detects organization role changes, role mapping changes, federation setting changes, and organization membership restriction changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization Service Account Secret Risk [table]: Detects expired or expiring organization service account secrets and maximum secret validity changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Organization UI or Public API Access List Change [table]: Detects organization UI IP access list disabling/enabling and public API access-list policy changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Service Account Event Observed [table]: Detects MongoDB Atlas service account lifecycle, role, secret, group-assignment, and access-list events from the Atlas events endpoints.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Cloud Backups - Backup Failure Status [table]: Detects backup snapshot records with failed, canceled, expired, or fallback failure statuses.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - Cluster Client Log Redaction Disabled [table]: Detects clusters where client log redaction is disabled.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - Cluster Paused [table]: Detects clusters in a paused state.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - Cluster Unsafe Protection Settings [table]: Detects clusters with point-in-time restore, termination protection, or client-log redaction disabled.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Clusters - MongoBleed Affected MongoDB Version Observed [table]: Detects MongoDB Server versions affected by CVE-2025-14847 / MongoBleed in cluster inventory. Atlas was patched by MongoDB, but this flags any reported affected version for review.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Custom Database Roles - Dangerous Custom Database Role Action [table]: Detects custom database roles granting dangerous administrative or destructive actions.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Database Users - High Privilege Database User [table]: Detects Atlas database users with broad administrative MongoDB roles.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Network Access - Temporary Network Access Entry [table]: Detects temporary Atlas network access entries with deleteAfterDate set.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Network Access - World Open Network Access Entry [table]: Detects Atlas network access list entries open to the Internet.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Organization Users - Organization Owner User Present [table]: Detects organization users with owner role assignments for review.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Organization Users - Pending or Invited Organization User [table]: Detects organization users with invited or pending membership states.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Programmatic API Keys - High Privilege API Key [table]: Detects programmatic API keys with owner/admin-style roles.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Alert Configuration Tampering [table]: Detects project activity where alert configurations are changed, disabled, enabled, or deleted.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - API Key Lifecycle or Permission Change [table]: Detects Atlas API key creation, deletion, project membership changes, role changes, description changes, or access-list inheritance changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Atlas Log Download [table]: Detects MongoDB, mongot, or BI Connector log downloads from Atlas.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Backup Control Plane Change [table]: Detects backup compliance disablement, restore requests, snapshot deletion, retention changes, schedule updates, and key backup credential changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Cloud Provider Access Credential Change [table]: Detects AWS IAM role, Azure service principal, or GCP service account changes used for Atlas cloud provider access.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Custom Database Role Lifecycle Change [table]: Detects MongoDB custom database role creation, deletion, or update events.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Database User Lifecycle Change [table]: Detects MongoDB database user creation, deletion, update, or X.509 certificate creation/revocation events.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Maintenance Control Weakened [table]: Detects maintenance deferral, protected hours changes, or maintenance auto-defer changes that can affect patch cadence.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - MongoDB Employee Support Access [table]: Detects MongoDB employee SSH sessions or temporary infrastructure access bypass events.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Network Permission Entry Change [table]: Detects Atlas project network permission entries being added, removed, or updated.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Observability Export Disabled or Changed [table]: Detects S3, OTel, or host external log export changes that could reduce monitoring coverage.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Project Security Checkup Degraded [table]: Detects project events indicating security checkup failures, exposed hosts, or security checkup alert configuration changes.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Project Activity Events - Resource Policy Violation or Change [table]: Detects resource policy creation, deletion, modification, or violation events.  
    - AlertQuery - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Service Accounts - High Privilege Service Account [table]: Detects service accounts with owner/admin-style roles.  
- Naming Schema: *AlertQuery - MongoDB Atlas - MongoDB Atlas - Admin API - Atlas Events - Open Critical Atlas Alert [Visualization - if any]*  

***  

## 9. [Templates](#9-templates)  

- Purpose: Templates are special objects which define a Gravwell query containing variables.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/templates/templates.html>)  
- Total: ***7***  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Investigation - Count by Event Type [numbercard]: This is intended to show a numbercard of MongoDB Atlas events by Atlas eventTypeName, alert typeName, metricName, auth result, or state name.  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Investigation - Count by Priority [numbercard]: This is intended to show a numbercard of MongoDB Atlas events by computed alert priority for the user, IP/CIDR, scope, or event type that you are investigating.  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Investigation - Count by Status [numbercard]: This is intended to show a numbercard of MongoDB Atlas events by Atlas alert status, auth result, configuration state, or cluster state.  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Investigation - Recent Events [table]: This is intended to show recent MongoDB Atlas alert, activity, access, identity, network, backup, and cluster events for an investigation.  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - Admin API - Investigation - Total Events [numbercard]: This is intended to show a numbercard of total MongoDB Atlas Admin API events for the user, IP/CIDR, scope, or event type that you are investigating within the time frame that you specify.  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Category [chart]: Displays a chart of events by category and subcategory for the category entered into the variable. - MongoDB - Options: Access,Activity,Events,Alerts,Authentication,Backups,Clusters,Database Users,Network Access,Organization,Projects,Service Accounts  
    - Template - MongoDB - Atlas - System - Log Types - Category [table]: Displays a table of events by category and subcategory for the category entered into the variable. - MongoDB - Options: Access,Activity,Events,Alerts,Authentication,Backups,Clusters,Database Users,Network Access,Organization,Projects,Service Accounts  

***  

## 10. [Dashboards](#10-dashboards)  

- Purpose: Dashboards are Gravwell’s way of showing the results from multiple searches at the same time.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/dashboards/dashboards.html>)  
- Total: ***18***  
    - MongoDB Atlas Category Overview: This Dashboard is a category overview of your MongoDB Atlas logs.  
    - MongoDB Atlas General Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of your MongoDB Atlas logs by tag, category, and subcategory.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Admin API Overview: Overview dashboard for MongoDB Atlas Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Access Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas access Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Activity Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas activity Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Alert Configs Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas alert configs Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Alerts Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas alerts Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas API Keys Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas api keys Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Backups Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas backups Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Clusters Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas clusters Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Custom Roles Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas custom roles Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Database Users Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas database users Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Network Access Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas network access Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Org Activity Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas org activity Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Org Users Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas org users Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Projects Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas projects Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Service Accounts Overview: This Dashboard is a general overview of MongoDB Atlas service accounts Admin API data.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Investigation: Investigate MongoDB Atlas Admin API alerts and high-signal activity by user/API key/service account, IP/CIDR, project or organization scope, and Atlas event type.  

#### 10.1. [Actionables](#10-1-actionables)  

- Purpose: Actionables provide a way to create custom menus that key on any text rendered in a query; users can take different actions on that text by selecting options in the menus.  
- [Documentation](<https://docs.gravwell.io/gui/actionables/actionables.html>)  
- Total: ***4***  
    - MongoDB Atlas User: MongoDB Atlas Actions on username, API key public key, service account client ID, or acknowledging username to launch the MongoDB Atlas Investigation dashboard.  
    - MongoDB Atlas IP: MongoDB Atlas Actions on IP address or CIDR block to launch the MongoDB Atlas Investigation dashboard.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Project or Organization: MongoDB Atlas Actions on project groupId or organization orgId to launch the MongoDB Atlas Investigation dashboard.  
    - MongoDB Atlas Event Type: MongoDB Atlas Actions on eventTypeName, alert typeName, or metricName to launch the MongoDB Atlas Investigation dashboard.  

